1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
My hallway lights turned on at 3am.
I had no idea why.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Home Assistant's own trace: cryptic node paths,
a run that "finished in 0.00 seconds", only 5 kept.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Home Assistant couldn't tell me.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
So I gave my house an APM.
Every automation run becomes a SigNoz flame graph.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Four saved views — one per failure archetype.
Open the "3am mystery".

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:53,000
There it is: a trigger fired a choose branch whose
condition passed SILENTLY — now a clickable named span.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The log line and the trace are one click apart.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The sidecar narrates itself: every "converted run"
log carries the trace_id it produced.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
A 47-second wait, hiding in plain sight.

10
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Morning routine: a single wait_for_trigger span,
~52s wide, dominates the whole run.

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Parallel branches. A repeat loop. A real error.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Good Night: overlapping parallel bars, stacked repeat
iterations, and a red ERROR span (divide-by-zero).

13
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Or just ask your house.

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Plain English in, one grounded sentence out — via the
SigNoz MCP server — each with a trace_id and flame-graph link.

15
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
One board for the whole house.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Question-titled panels and a $room selector that
refocuses every panel at once.

17
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:44,000
A service map of your house — the failing path to
persistent_notification flagged in red.

18
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
And it tells Home Assistant when something breaks.

19
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:57,000
A traces-based rule, "Automation failing", is firing
on the error spans.

20
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:06,000
The loop closes: the SigNoz [FIRING] alert lands as a
notification back inside Home Assistant.

21
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Home Assistant always had traces.
It just never let anyone see them.

22
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Give your house an APM.
github.com/wiz-abhi/home-apm · foundryctl cast -f casting.yaml
